cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use incident2chaos or its corpus, please cite the software and paper 1."
title: "incident2chaos: chaos experiments derived from real cloud incident reports"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ramaswamy
    given-names: Yogesh
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4261-5785"
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/yogeshramaswamy608/incident2chaos"
keywords:
  - chaos engineering
  - fault injection
  - incident analysis
  - postmortems
  - Chaos Mesh
  - LitmusChaos
abstract: >-
  A command line tool that turns a post-incident report, coded under a published
  codebook of 13 trigger codes and 20 fault classes, into Chaos Mesh or LitmusChaos
  experiments marked as direct injections, approximations or not injectable, with the
  coded corpus of 497 public cloud post-incident reports and a coverage command that
  reruns the measurement of paper 1.
